    "manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:150-200;3827;3831;3862;3869 — partial file; complete required excerpt. Target-label search across all 50 manuscript TeX files returned all 11 relevant labels within the fully read sources or required excerpt."
  ],
  "checks": [
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DriverParameters.Homog: H:homog",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:20-22 states 'd = 1 ∨ d = 2 ∨ d = 3', '0 < a', 'a < 1', 'a + alpha < 2', and '(0 < alpha ∧ alpha < d) ∨ (alpha = d ∧ d = 1)'. TeX manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:169-185 gives precisely these numerical hypotheses, with a = alpha_0. The omission of covariance, spectral and scaling data is explicitly identified as a parameter-only generalization in candidate/statement-ledger.md:493-502. lean/claims.yaml:720-726 faithfully summarizes the definition."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DriverParameters.gamma_interval_nonempty: E:driver-parameters",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:25-26 assumes 'h : Homog d alpha a' and concludes existence of '0 < γ ∧ γ < min (1 / 2) ((2 - alpha) / 2)'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:5-6 retains 'H:homog', and :18-23 gives the identical strict gamma interval and asserts nonemptiness. candidate/statement-ledger.md:493-503 discloses the dropped covariance hypotheses; lean/claims.yaml:727-733 matches the Lean type."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DriverParameters.theta_beta_interval_nonempty: E:driver-parameters",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:33-34 assumes 'h : Homog d alpha a' and concludes '∃ θ β', with '1 / 2 < θ ∧ θ < β ∧ β < min (1 - a / 2) ((3 - a - alpha) / 2)'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:5-6,18-23 retains H:homog and states the same chain and nonemptiness. The parameter-only generalization is disclosed at candidate/statement-ledger.md:493-498; its row :504 and lean/claims.yaml:734-740 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.DriverParameters.parameters_nonempty: E:driver-parameters",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:44-46 assumes 'h : Homog d alpha a' and concludes simultaneous existence of 'γ θ β' satisfying both strict chains. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:5-6,18-23 retains H:homog and says 'The strict intervals are nonempty.' Constants, strictness and simultaneous existence agree. candidate/statement-ledger.md:493-505 and lean/claims.yaml:741-747 accurately describe the parameter-only statement."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianScalarPowers.weighted_power: L:gaussian-scalar-powers",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GaussianScalarPowers.lean:29-31 assumes '0 < θ', 'θ < 1', '0 ≤ u', '0 ≤ v'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:14-16 states '0 < θ < 1' and 'u,v ≥ 0', with the same weighted-power inequality. candidate/statement-ledger.md:519 and lean/claims.yaml:643-649 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianScalarPowers.integer_power: L:gaussian-scalar-powers",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GaussianScalarPowers.lean:37-39 uses '(L q : ℕ)', '0 < L', 'q ≤ L', and arbitrary real x,y. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:18-22 uses integers 'L > 0' and '0 ≤ q ≤ L', with real x,y and identical weights and powers; :34-35 explicitly includes endpoint powers with a^0 = 1. candidate/statement-ledger.md:520 and lean/claims.yaml:650-656 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianScalarPowers.finite_holder: L:gaussian-scalar-powers",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GaussianScalarPowers.lean:66-70 assumes a finite set, '1 < m', and '0 ≤ a i', '0 ≤ b i' on it. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:24-25 states finite Hölder for 'nonnegative finite sequences' with exponents m and m/(m-1), 'm > 1'; its normalization proof :37-41 confirms the usual conclusion. Exponents and zero cases agree. candidate/statement-ledger.md:521 and lean/claims.yaml:657-663 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GaussianScalarPowers.expectation_rpow_le: L:gaussian-scalar-powers",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GaussianScalarPowers.lean:91-94 assumes '[IsProbabilityMeasure μ]', 'Integrable Z μ', '0 ≤ᵐ[μ] Z', and '0 < r < 1'; it proves integrability and the expectation bound. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:25-26 says 'Z ≥ 0 has finite expectation F' and '0 < r < 1'; :41-43 uses 'almost surely' and expectation of the constant one. Thus probability, integrability and almost-everywhere interpretation are genuine implicit conditions, explicitly recorded at candidate/statement-ledger.md:509-522 and lean/claims.yaml:664-670."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.gram_scalar_algebra_paper: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:82-89 assumes '[CompleteSpace H]', a finite index type, 'C i j = inner ℝ (k i) (k j)', and '0 ≤ C i j'; its scalar component quantifies arbitrary real ell, '0 < w' and '0 ≤ t'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4-6 supplies a real Hilbert space, finite indices and the same Gram hypotheses; :26-36 states all three conclusions with real ell, w > 0, t ≥ 0. The ell_i,b_i families in the score setup do not occur in this lemma's conclusions, and their nonuse is expressly disclosed at candidate/statement-ledger.md:528-532. The row :538 and lean/claims.yaml:776-782 match the wrapper."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.sqrt_dual: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:32-33 assumes arbitrary real ell, '0 < w', '0 ≤ t'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:27-29 says 'For real ell, w > 0 and t ≥ 0' and gives the identical inequality. candidate/statement-ledger.md:539 and lean/claims.yaml:671-677 accurately summarize it; the paragraph :528-532 explains the unused ambient hypotheses."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.hilbert_square: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:56-59 assumes a real inner product space and arbitrary 'Φ z : H', concluding the equality and ensuing inequality as a conjunction. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4,31-34 assumes a real Hilbert space and 'Φ,z ∈ H', with the identical chain and factors 1/2. The completeness generalization is explicit at candidate/statement-ledger.md:528-532; row :540 and lean/claims.yaml:692-698 are faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.hilbert_square_eq: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:41-43 assumes a real inner product space and 'Φ z : H'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4,31-34 uses a real Hilbert space and 'Φ,z ∈ H'. The equality is identical; dropping completeness is expressly disclosed at candidate/statement-ledger.md:528-532. Row :541 and lean/claims.yaml:678-684 correctly identify only the identity component."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.hilbert_square_le: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:49-51 assumes a real inner product space and 'Φ z : H', concluding '<Φ,z> - ‖Φ‖²/2 ≤ ‖z‖²/2'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4,31-34 uses a real Hilbert space and gives the same inequality by its equality chain. The disclosed completeness generalization is valid. candidate/statement-ledger.md:542 and lean/claims.yaml:685-691 faithfully describe the inequality component."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.GramScalarAlgebra.gram_identity: L:gram-scalar-algebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:66-70 assumes finite indices, a real inner product space, 'C i j = inner ℝ (k i) (k j)', and arbitrary real weights. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4-6,36 has finite indices, a real Hilbert space, the same definition of C and finite real weights. The norm-square identity is identical. Omitting completeness and entrywise nonnegativity is explicitly disclosed at candidate/statement-ledger.md:528-532. Row :543 and lean/claims.yaml:699-705 match."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.KappaRange.kappa: E:kappa",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/KappaRange.lean:22 defines '(4 - alpha - alpha0) / (3 - alpha)' without hypotheses. TeX manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:188-190 defines the identical expression in the standing H:homog context :169-185. candidate/statement-ledger.md:555 and lean/claims.yaml:706-712 claim the formula, not an unconditional range; the following theorem supplies the admissible-domain range."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.KappaRange.kappa_mem_Ioo: E:kappa",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/KappaRange.lean:26-29 assumes 'd = 1 ∨ d = 2 ∨ d = 3', '0 < alpha0 < 1', 'alpha0 + alpha < 2', and '(0 < alpha ∧ alpha < d) ∨ (alpha = d ∧ d = 1)', concluding membership in 'Set.Ioo 1 2'. TeX manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:169-190 supplies those parameters plus covariance data and states κ ∈ (1,2). candidate/statement-ledger.md:547-556 accurately discloses the parameter-only generalization; lean/claims.yaml:713-719 matches."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.RayleighTail.rayleigh_tail_paper: L:tube-rayleigh-tail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:178-185 assumes 'Measurable G', growth for '0 ≤ r', '0 ≤ C', '1 < ν < 2', '0 < δ', 'δ < 1', '0 < M', and '4 * C ≤ M ^ (2 - ν)'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:8-9 fixes '0 < δ < 1'; :455-461 gives Borel G, the same growth, exponent and cutoff conditions, and exactly '4 exp((A0-M²/4)/δ)'. The halfline domain is supported by :182, and head finiteness by :476-477. candidate/statement-ledger.md:560-572 and lean/claims.yaml:783-789 accurately disclose the real-domain representation and omitted application."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.RayleighTail.rayleigh_tail: L:tube-rayleigh-tail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:91-97 assumes measurable G, growth on '0 ≤ r', '0 ≤ C', '1 < ν < 2', '0 < δ', '0 < M', and the same cutoff. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:8-9,455-461 has the additional standing 'δ < 1', with identical integral and constant 4. candidate/statement-ledger.md:564-573 explicitly identifies this generalization and the unformalized application. lean/claims.yaml:769-775 faithfully summarizes the type."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.RayleighTail.rayleigh_head_integrable: L:tube-rayleigh-tail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:146-149 assumes 'Measurable G', growth on '0 ≤ r', '0 ≤ C', '1 < ν', '0 < δ', and '0 < M'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:455-457,476-477 asserts finiteness on [0,M] under the lemma's stronger hypotheses, using 'G(r) ≤ A0 + C M^ν'. candidate/statement-ledger.md:574 expressly notes that ν < 2 and the cutoff are unnecessary; :564 identifies the delta generalization. lean/claims.yaml:762-768 is faithful."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.RayleighTail.cutoff_split: L:tube-rayleigh-tail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:32-35 assumes '0 < M', 'M ≤ r', '0 ≤ C', '1 < ν', 'ν < 2', and '4 * C ≤ M ^ (2 - ν)'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:468-472 explicitly lists these exact scalar conditions and concludes 'Cr^ν-r²/2 ≤ -M²/8-r²/8'. candidate/statement-ledger.md:575 and lean/claims.yaml:748-754 correctly map this to the proof step."
    },
    {
      "claim": "StratonovichHAMSecondMoment.RayleighTail.gaussian_weight_tail: L:tube-rayleigh-tail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:54-57 assumes '0 < δ', '0 ≤ M', and proves integrability and integral '4 * exp(-M²/(8δ))'. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:8-9,457,472-475 uses '0 < δ < 1', 'M > 0' and the same antiderivative and tail value. candidate/statement-ledger.md:564,576 and lean/claims.yaml:755-761 explicitly state the broader endpoint and delta ranges. Open versus closed integration endpoints do not change the Lebesgue integral."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-DriverParameters",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:493-498 cites the correct source, whose manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:5-6 retains H:homog and :18-23 asserts nonemptiness. The paragraph correctly describes lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:20-46 as a numerical generalization and accurately identifies the parameters actually used."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-GaussianScalarPowers",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:509-515 accurately covers all four parts of manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:13-44 and lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GaussianScalarPowers.lean:29-94. Probability, finite expectation as integrability, almost-everywhere nonnegativity and the proved power integrability are justified by the TeX proof, not merely asserted by the ledger."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-GramScalarAlgebra",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:526-534 accurately identifies manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:4-6,26-49, the generalized inner-product statements, and the Hilbert/nonnegative-Gram wrapper at lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/GramScalarAlgebra.lean:82-89. It expressly identifies the unused score parameters ell_i,b_i; the lemma itself quantifies an unrestricted scalar ell."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-KappaRange",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:547-551 accurately maps the formula and both strict inequalities to manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:169-190, and honestly describes lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/KappaRange.lean:22-29 as a parameter-only generalization."
    },
    {
      "claim": "PARA-RayleighTail",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:560-568 accurately distinguishes the general delta-positive results from the delta-less-than-one wrapper, explains the domain representation, includes head and tail integrability, and excludes the application at manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:463-464,477-478. The Lean types at lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/RayleighTail.lean:91-97,146-149,178-185 support these statements."
    },
    {
      "claim": "LEDGER-INDEX",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:97-102 lists exactly the 21 declarations in the five module tables :502-576, with matching labels. An unrestricted target-label search across all 50 manuscript TeX files found every relevant label: manuscript/notes/integrated_compact_gaussian.tex:13,15,20; manuscript/notes/integrated_positive_gram.tex:26,28,32; manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:18; manuscript/notes/integrated_gaussian_tubes.tex:455,458; manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:169,189."
    },
    {
      "claim": "LEDGER-TOTALS",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "Counting the declaration rows in all per-module tables of candidate/statement-ledger.md:108-576 gives 109 rows: 8 definitions and 101 theorems, with 61 labelled and 48 unlabelled. The five new sections contribute 21 rows, including two definitions. These counts agree with :105-106 and the kinds in lean/claims.yaml:1-789."
    },
    {
      "claim": "COVERAGE-ROWS",
      "verdict": "FAIL",
      "reason": "The Gaussian, Gram and Rayleigh rows at lean/coverage.yaml:101-117,185-194 cite appropriate declarations and accurately scope the Rayleigh omission. However, E:driver-parameters at :27-35 and E:kappa at :36-44 are both classified 'same-assumptions' while citing only parameter-only generalizations. Their notes acknowledge the discrepancy but do not cure the false class under the review contract. Neither cited declaration includes the manuscript's covariance hypotheses. See W1 and W2."
    },
    {
      "claim": "SCOPE-PROSE",
      "verdict": "PASS",
      "reason": "candidate/statement-ledger.md:29-42 accurately distinguishes Gaussian manuscript hypotheses, generalized Gram/Rayleigh results with paper wrappers, and the two parameter-only generalizations. It expressly excludes the Rayleigh application and explains implicit analytic side conditions. This prose is accurate independently of the contradictory coverage classifications identified in W1 and W2."
    }
  ],
  "findings": {
    "fatal": [
      "W1 — E:driver-parameters coverage misclassification. lean/coverage.yaml:31 says 'class: same-assumptions' and :33 cites parameters_nonempty, but Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/DriverParameters.lean:44 assumes only '(h : Homog d alpha a)', whose definition :20-22 contains numerical conditions alone. TeX manuscript/notes/integrated_actual_operator_driver.tex:5-6 says 'Retain Hypothesis H:homog'; manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:171-180 additionally requires covariance and spectral measures and covariance scaling. The coverage note :34-35 correctly calls this a generalization, contradicting its class. Fix the coverage classification to explicitly represent a parameter-only generalization rather than same-assumptions, or cite a new wrapper that actually states the full manuscript hypotheses.",
      "W2 — E:kappa coverage misclassification. lean/coverage.yaml:42 says 'class: same-assumptions' and :41 cites kappa_mem_Ioo. Lean lean/StratonovichHAMSecondMoment/KappaRange.lean:26-28 assumes only 'hd', 'h0', 'h1', 'hthr' and 'halpha', all numerical. TeX manuscript/notes/notes_stratonovich_ham_second_moment.tex:169-190 states the exponent range in the standing homogeneous-covariance context, including the measure and scaling hypotheses at :171-180. The coverage note :43-44 acknowledges that those hypotheses are not modelled. Fix the coverage classification to explicitly represent a parameter-only generalization rather than same-assumptions, or cite a new wrapper with the full manuscript hypotheses."
    ],
    "major": [],
    "minor": []
  },
  "required_repairs": [
    "Resolve W1: remove the false same-assumptions classification for E:driver-parameters by classifying the cited statement as a parameter-only generalization, or supply and cite a genuinely manuscript-hypothesis wrapper.",
    "Resolve W2: remove the false same-assumptions classification for E:kappa by classifying the cited statement as a parameter-only generalization, or supply and cite a genuinely manuscript-hypothesis wrapper."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "All complete-reading requirement A sources and the full required main-manuscript excerpt were read. The remainder of the main manuscript and other TeX inputs were not substantively reviewed; all 50 inputs were searched for the relevant labels.",
    "Compilation, absence of sorry and the axiom restriction were supplied premises, not independently reproduced. This review concerns correspondence, not kernel proof verification.",
    "The provenance record was read; its supervisor-checked byte binding was accepted rather than independently reconstructed.",
    "This AI review is neither human verification nor a novelty audit. Previously reviewed ledger rows were read for totals but not re-audited for mathematical correspondence."
  ]
}
